I am really embarrassed, but I wanted to write how I fixed the issue, so people can see this and try what I didn't<br><br>I did not have access to another computer to assuming this was a driver issue, I just deleted my disks and reinstalled everything in my mind making it equivalent to another computer as VK3KYY suggested. The issue did not go away and when I talked with the seller on how they managed to fix it they just told me that they flashed the original firmware and it worked. I thought they were not telling me how they did it since the Turkish language firmware is their licensed product and did not want to share the details with me. I decided to get a completely new computer just to try it before sending it in one more time, and it worked. Then I switched the USB port on my computer and it worked. My radio is to the left of my device where there is only a single USB port and since my MD 390 device flashed fine from that port I never tried unplugging and moving the radio to the right-hand side using the other ports.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7273">TA2EGG</a> — Thu Feb 06, 2025 3:21 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
