		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4821&amp;p=35586#p35586"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I believe a non-standard bootloader is the issue I am just upset that it used to work when I installed it 2-3 months prior and worked without issue. I searched online for the original bootloader file to no avail do you have access to the bootloader or can you point me to the files. I don't think they will agree to installing OpenGD77 but I will try my luck. Thank you for your support.</div></blockquote>What hardware version of MD9600 do you have.<br><br>I think there may be more than one version of the MD9600, depending on the hardware version, but the OpenGD77CPS works with all normal versions of bootloader regardless of hardware version.<br><br><br>Someone will need to backup the MCU memory in their radio and post the file somewhere, because I don't have access to a MD9600 to do this at the moment<br><br><br><br>You will also need to open the radio and connect a hardware debugger to the CPU, e.g. a STLink.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Wed Feb 05, 2025 6:59 am</p><hr />
