<blockquote class="uncited"><div>The seller was able to restore the original firmware in Turkish to the device but when I tried to flash OpenGD77 again the same issue happened.</div></blockquote>Possibly there is something non-standard with your radio.<br><br>Or you have some problem on your computer.<br><br>Did you ask the seller to install OpenGD77? i.e this will eliminate the possibility that the problem is your computer or PSU etc.<br><br><br>On rare occasions people have bought from suppliers who have custom commercial versions of various radios, and these may have a different bootloader which prevents non-official firmware being loaded.<br><br>The only way to install the firmware onto these non-standard radios is to directly connect to the hardware debug port pads on the PCB (SWD), and install a standard bootloader.<br><br>However I can only remember 1 person having one of these special radios, and I can't remember if it was a MD9600 /RT90 or a handheld<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Tue Feb 04, 2025 9:44 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
